.\" FreeBASIC NuttX SDK
.\" -------------------
.\" File: nuttx-riscv32-qemu-smoke.1
.\" Purpose: Document the installed RISC-V NuttX QEMU smoke-test driver.
.\" Responsibilities: Describe program selection, workspace control, and emulation.
.\" This file intentionally does not list every specialized device assertion.
.\"
.TH NUTTX-RISCV32-QEMU-SMOKE 1 "2026-07-30" "FreeBASIC NuttX SDK" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nuttx-riscv32-qemu-smoke \- build and test a FreeBASIC NuttX program in QEMU
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nuttx-riscv32-qemu-smoke
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nuttx-riscv32-qemu-smoke
prepares a RISC-V NuttX workspace, builds a selected FreeBASIC program into
the firmware image, runs the image with qemu-system-riscv32, and checks the
captured console output for the requested smoke-test conditions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --nuttx-workdir " DIR"
Use the specified NuttX and apps workspace.
.TP
.B --update
Update existing NuttX source trees.
.TP
.B --no-bootstrap
Require an already prepared workspace.
.TP
.B --prepare-only
Prepare the workspace without building or running QEMU.
.TP
.BI --bas " FILE"
Compile the selected FreeBASIC source file.
.TP
.BI --generated-c " FILE"
Use existing generated C instead of invoking the FreeBASIC compiler.
.TP
.BI --extra-c " FILE"
Add a C support source to the NuttX application. This option may be repeated.
.TP
.BI --extra-cxx " FILE"
Add a C++ support source to the application.
.TP
.BI --extra-asm " FILE"
Add an assembly support source to the application.
.TP
.BI --app-name " NAME"
Set the NuttX application name.
.TP
.B --with-gfxlib
Link the selected NuttX graphics support objects.
.TP
.B --sfx-no-media-decoders
Link sound support without bundled media decoders.
.TP
.BI --qemu-storage-root " DIR"
Exercise a temporary NuttX storage mount at the selected path.
.TP
.BR --qemu-storage-backend " " tmpfs | virtio-blk
Select the emulated storage backend.
.TP
.B --qemu-usb-root-devices
Attach the supported USB smoke devices directly to xHCI root ports.
.TP
.B --qemu-usb-hub-devices
Attach the supported USB smoke devices through an emulated hub.
.TP
.B --help
Show the complete device, network, timeout, and assertion option reference.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fbc (1),
.BR fbc-nuttx-esp32p4 (1)
.\"
.\" end of nuttx-riscv32-qemu-smoke.1
